---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro"
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Feature requests · Threa Developers"
  description="Where to ask for missing Threa API endpoints, scopes, or integrations: file an issue on the threahq/threa GitHub repository."
  current="feature-requests"
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Feature requests</p>
  <h1>Something <span class="accent">missing</span>?</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    The API is small on purpose and grows in the open. If there's an endpoint,
    scope, or integration you need, file it. Threa is public source, so requests
    go to the issue tracker.
  </p>

  <p>
    The form below opens a prefilled issue on the public repo for you to review
    and submit. You can also browse what's already been requested before adding
    yours.
  </p>

  <form class="fr-form" id="fr-form">
    <div class="row">
      <label for="fr-title">One-line summary</label>
      <input id="fr-title" type="text" required placeholder="e.g. Bulk export endpoint for memos" />
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <label for="fr-area">Area</label>
      <select id="fr-area">
        <option>Public API</option>
        <option>Bot runtime / agents</option>
        <option>Memos &amp; search</option>
        <option>Auth &amp; keys</option>
        <option>MCP server</option>
        <option>Other</option>
      </select>
    </div>
    <div class="row">
      <label for="fr-use">What are you trying to do?</label>
      <textarea id="fr-use" placeholder="The task, not the solution. What's the workflow this would unblock?"></textarea>
    </div>
    <button type="submit" class="cta">Open a GitHub issue</button>
  </form>

  <p style="margin-top:18px;">
    Prefer to look first?
    <a class="link" href="https://github.com/threahq/threa/issues">Browse open issues</a>
    on <code>threahq/threa</code>.
  </p>

  <div class="note">
    <strong>Already requested</strong>
    A bulk export endpoint, an MCP server, and outbound webhooks come up most
    often. A thumbs-up on an existing issue helps us order the queue.
  </div>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      const form = document.getElementById("fr-form")
      if (!form) return
      form.addEventListener("submit", function (e) {
        e.preventDefault()
        const title = (document.getElementById("fr-title")).value.trim()
        const area = (document.getElementById("fr-area")).value
        const use = (document.getElementById("fr-use")).value.trim()
        if (!title) return
        const body =
          "**Area:** " + area + "\n\n" +
          "**What I'm trying to do**\n" + (use || "_(describe the workflow)_") + "\n\n" +
          "---\n_Filed from the developer docs._"
        const url =
          "https://github.com/threahq/threa/issues/new" +
          "?title=" + encodeURIComponent(title) +
          "&body=" + encodeURIComponent(body) +
          "&labels=" + encodeURIComponent("enhancement")
        window.open(url, "_blank", "noopener")
      })
    })()
  </script>
</DocsLayout>
